  installed host helper `/usr/local/libexec/omniroute-deploy.py` was not read
  or modified; TL316 host update is recorded in repo `openspec/TODO.md`.
- `ESBUILD_BINARY_PATH=/tmp/tl315-esbuild-linux-x64/node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild`
  focused migration/benchmark/capability command passed 87/87. Artifact-index
  upgrade test passed 2/2. Deploy-helper tests passed 58/58. Combined overlay,
  layout, and verifier tests passed 20/20 after correcting the stale assertion.
- The overlay policy finding was a test-contract defect: `.dockerignore`
  intentionally unignores only `tests/unit/build/model-benchmark-search-runtime-resolution.test.mjs`
  plus its required parent directories; Dockerfile copies that one smoke into
  the candidate. The test now asserts exactly those four negations.
- The repo deploy verifier compares both candidate and prior-image
  `org.opencontainers.image.base.digest` labels to its constant, confirming
  the repository value must track the new OCI index. The installed host helper
  still requires TL316 review/install before deployment; no deployment action
  was performed.
- Code Simplifier review found the explicit allowlist comparison and release
  pin assertions clear and bounded; no further simplification needed. No full
  suite or strict OpenSpec CLI validation was run. Independent review, baseline
  comparison, host-helper update, local commit, and TL313 migration rehearsal
  remain open.

